<description>
Recolor each closed orthogonal line loop so convex bend pixels are yellow and concave bend pixels are red.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background and exactly one foreground color.
- The foreground forms one or more 4-connected one-pixel-wide closed cycles; every foreground pixel has degree 2.
Rule
- Trace each cycle and inspect the turn at each foreground pixel.
- Straight pixels keep the original foreground color.
- Bend pixels whose turn direction is the majority direction for that cycle are convex corners and become yellow.
- Bend pixels whose turn direction is the minority direction for that cycle are concave corners and become red.
Key insight
- A simple rectilinear closed boundary has exactly four more convex bends than concave bends, so convexity can be inferred structurally from the majority turn sign within each traced cycle.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "monochrome one-cell-wide 4-connected closed orthogonal cycles on the background",
  "transform": "within each cycle, keep straight pixels in the original color; recolor bend pixels with the majority turn direction as yellow convex corners and bend pixels with the minority turn direction as red concave corners"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-15 rows x 13-16 cols
  background: 0
  foreground: single color from {1,3,5,6,7,8,9} (not 0, 2, or 4)
  cycles:
    count: 2-3 non-overlapping, non-nested, simply-connected rectilinear closed loops
    structure: 1-pixel-wide 4-connected; every pixel has exactly degree 2
    perimeter_pixels: 8-42 per cycle
    convex_corners: 4-12 (majority turn direction)
    concave_corners: 0-8 (minority turn direction)
    invariant: convex - concave = 4 always
    min_gap_between_cycles: >=2 (Manhattan distance)
    bbox: 3x3 to 10x12 per cycle
    interior: single connected region of background pixels [observed]
  output_transform: |
    Straight pixels (no turn) keep foreground color.
    Convex bend pixels (majority turn sign per cycle) become yellow (4).
    Concave bend pixels (minority turn sign per cycle) become red (2).

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction of rectilinear cycles
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size and foreground color per spec.
    2. For each cycle (2-3 total), generate a simply-connected rectilinear polygon
       boundary by starting with a rectangle and adding/removing rectangular notches
       to create concave corners. Ensure every boundary pixel has exactly degree 2.
    3. Place cycles on grid with no overlap and Manhattan gap >=2 between any pair.
       Bounding boxes must not nest.
    4. Verify each cycle has convex - concave = 4 (guaranteed by simple-connectivity).
    5. Fill grid background with 0, cycle pixels with foreground color.
```
</generation_spec>
